# Morsel for the God

**Key:** D minor
**Tempo:** 72 BPM (verses) / 108 BPM (chorus)
**Style:** Quiet verses, explosive choruses (Pixies/Nirvana dynamic)

---

**VERSE 1**
*(Clean guitar, sparse bass, whispered/spoken)*

Charnel dust and copper air
Leprous light on cyclopean walls
I remember golden hair
Sunlight dying as the darkness calls

Dragged through stone by fur-clad hands
Pinioned arms and trembling lips
Defiance melts in terror's fire
As tenebrous velvet folds and slips

**PRE-CHORUS**
*(Building tension, distortion creeping in)*

The silence hums like dead cosmos
Geological slumber stirs
Two phosphorescent slits expose
A gaze both ravenous and bored

**CHORUS**
*(Full distortion, drums crash, screamed/belted)*

Another morsel, another morsel
The god weighs flesh upon his throne
Stringy, garrulous—less than tolerable
Your prayers dissolve in lightless stone

The slothful maw, obsidian tide
Drinks the essence, drains the soul
Primordial entropy can't be denied
You're just a morsel—swallowed whole

**VERSE 2**
*(Return to quiet, haunted delivery)*

Quicksilver black, liquefied night
Pours across my screaming face
The amber sun, my lover's light
Rendered obscene in this charnel place

No tearing flesh, no splintering bone
Just a wet sibilant hiss
My vital essence drunk and gone
Consumed by the formless abyss

**PRE-CHORUS**
*(Building intensity)*

Fastidious critique of meat
The shrieking adds acidity
With ponderous certainty, entropy's beat
Measures out eternity

**CHORUS**
*(Full distortion, drums crash, screamed/belted)*

Another morsel, another morsel
The god weighs flesh upon his throne
Stringy, garrulous—less than tolerable
Your prayers dissolve in lightless stone

The slothful maw, obsidian tide
Drinks the essence, drains the soul
Primordial entropy can't be denied
You're just a morsel—swallowed whole

**BRIDGE**
*(Slow, doom-laden, bass-heavy)*

Parchment skin on hollow bone
Chartreuse vapor, crushed decay
Dragged like sticks to shadows thrown
The Voormis sweep the husk away

*(Spoken, echoing, over feedback)*

One does wish they'd consider
The manifold virtues
Of proper fattening

**FINAL CHORUS**
*(Explosive, then decaying)*

Another morsel, another morsel
Sempiternal slothfulness reigns
Tolerable, barely tolerable
Only the dripping water remains

**OUTRO**
*(Single clean guitar, fading)*

The sun I loved is lost to stone
A god who knows no pity waits
No meaning in my final moan
Just meat that feeds what slumbers and sates

*(Drums: single heartbeat hits, slowing, stopping)*

